<title>USA: Cargill finds buyer for North Korea-bound US wheat.</title>
<headline>Cargill finds buyer for North Korea-bound US wheat.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargill found an alternative buyer for 20,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat that was en route for North Korea when a zinc-for-wheat deal collapsed, a spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>She declined to name the new buyer. The wheat was on a ship that loaded on the West Coast a month ago.</p>
<p>&quot;It was en route,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>The ship reportedly was near North Korean waters when the barter collapsed. The spokeswoman declined to comment on the reports.</p>
</text>
